# Jazz Comping: Minor ii-V-i (repertoire plan: st-jazz-minor-ii-v). An original 16-bar study on
# the minor ii-V-i in A minor, as a bossa nova: Bm7b5 | E7 | Am7 | Am7, four times.
# Shapes: Bm7b5 (x2323x: B F A D), E7 (xx2434: E B D G#), Am7: the grip xx2213 (E A C G) with the
# open A string under it, so the box shows x02213.
# Bossa comping, fingerstyle, straight eighths: the thumb (p) plays the bass on beats 1 and 3,
# and i, m and a pluck the other three notes of the grip together. Over two bars the chords fall
# on 1, the "and" of 2 and 4, then on 2 and the "and" of 3. In Am7 the thumb alternates the
# open A (beat 1) and the E on string 4 fret 2 (beat 3).
# Bars 9-16: an 8-bar melody over the same chords, in seventh position (finger 1 on fret 7). Over
# E7 it uses A harmonic minor, with G# (string 2 fret 9) in place of G (string 2 fret 8); over
# Bm7b5 and Am7 the natural minor, with G. Bar 14 runs up E F G# A B: the step and a half from
# F to G# is the sound of harmonic minor.
title: Jazz Comping: Minor ii-V-i
